Both doors are wired. GuardedTool and ArcGuardedTool (the sub-agent chain, which receives none of with_truncation/with_recovery_hints/maybe_hook) each call the same helper. This repo's recurring "two doors, one policy, one deaf" failure is avoided.

**The always-wrap change is the load-bearing part, not an inefficiency.** `maybe_guard` used to return the bare tool when `restrictions.is_empty()`. Since the file-tool default is unrestricted, wiring the repair onto the old conditional wrapper would have made it unreachable for every default user. label/description/parameters_schema all delegate to inner, so always-wrapping is transparent to tool listing and MCP collision detection.

